==============================================================================
VERDICT
==============================================================================
  Fibre size 1 < 3 at q = (0, -1, -1), so the defect there is 2.
  Minimum defect observed over the probes : 2

  CONSEQUENCE.  (Q_2) -- 'Keller + at most 2 sheet(s) lost at infinity =>
  automorphism' -- is FALSE, witnessed by this map.  So the classical rung
  cannot be weakened to allow that many lost sheets; 'no loss' is sharp at
  that threshold.

  Independent of the outcome above, the structural point stands: rung 2 is
  stated along the DEFECT axis, and the lattice improves it along three OTHER
  axes -- Jelonek singularity type, Galois-ness, and the point-stabiliser
  condition.  A hypothesis can be unimprovable in its own direction and still
  sit near the bottom of the lattice.
